Subject: [PATCH] peer_mem: export IB peer memory API as GPL-only symbols

Ported from https://github.com/microsoft/azurelinux/pull/17512.

Kernels with the GPL-only symbol_get restriction reject runtime lookup of
the IB peer-memory API when it is exported with EXPORT_SYMBOL.

Unlike Azure Linux's prebuilt kmods, Non-AZL images rebuild DOCA and GPU
modules with DKMS. Exporting this API with EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL lets either
AMDGPU/DOCA build order work during system update: AMDGPU can link directly
when DOCA's matching Module.symvers is already present, or use runtime
symbol_request when it builds first. The latter needs the patched DOCA
provider at runtime, thus avoiding having to enforce DKMS build ordering.

This is especially important for AMD MI300X configurations lacking
DMA-BUF support. V100 is exempt because its proprietary nvidia-peermem
cannot use GPL-only exports.

---
 drivers/infiniband/core/peer_mem.c | 8 ++++----
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/infiniband/core/peer_mem.c b/drivers/infiniband/core/peer_mem.c
--- a/drivers/infiniband/core/peer_mem.c
+++ b/drivers/infiniband/core/peer_mem.c
@@ -89,4 +89,4 @@
 }
-EXPORT_SYMBOL(ib_register_peer_memory_client);
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(ib_register_peer_memory_client);
 
 void ib_unregister_peer_memory_client(void *reg_handle)
@@ -110,4 +110,4 @@
 }
-EXPORT_SYMBOL(ib_unregister_peer_memory_client);
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(ib_unregister_peer_memory_client);
 
 static struct ib_peer_memory_client *
@@ -320,4 +320,4 @@
 }
-EXPORT_SYMBOL(ib_umem_activate_invalidation_notifier);
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(ib_umem_activate_invalidation_notifier);
 
 /*
@@ -361,4 +361,4 @@
 }
-EXPORT_SYMBOL(ib_umem_stop_invalidation_notifier);
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(ib_umem_stop_invalidation_notifier);
 
 static void fix_peer_sgls(struct ib_umem_peer *umem_p,
